prepare your machine for ssh communication so you can use xTerm:
	sudo apt-get install ssh

prepare your machine for git and github:
	sudo apt-get install git-all
	ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "e-mail"  (server mail is liis.zef.irb@gmail.com, but use yours for your Linux machine)
	> Enter file in which to save the key (/c/Users/YOU/.ssh/id_ALGORITHM):[Press enter for default]
	> Enter passphrase (empty for no passphrase): [Press enter]
	> Enter same passphrase again: [Press enter]
	cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
Copy the complete cat output and login to github and click your icon in the top right -> settings -> SSH and GPG keys -> New SSH key:
Title: <anything>
Key type: Authentication Key
Key: <paste>
Add SSH key

git clone git@github.com:liis-zef-irb/installationScripts.git
cd installationScripts
chmod +x install_epics_on_ubuntu.sh
./install_epics_on_ubuntu.sh

relax... it will take more than half an hour..

